# What this file separates
#
# The folder on disk is both the working place and the extension. Everything
# needed to load, run, test and understand the extension is published; the
# working notes are not. The rule is an allowlist for `docs/`, not a list of
# exclusions: a note written next week is private by default, which is the safe
# direction. Adding a public document therefore means adding a line here.
#
# `CLAUDE.md` is deliberately published. It is the only document that explains
# why the code is shaped the way it is, and a contributor who does not have it
# will reopen decisions that were settled after a bug.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the notes
# Everything under docs/, then the few files that are part of the product.
docs/*
!docs/LIMITES.md

# Dated investigations, screenshots, audit captures, rejected experiments.
docs/audit-*/
docs/revue-ui/
experiments/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the leftovers
# Fixtures pulled from a real account while debugging.
test/.tmp-*

# Avatars `tools/shoot.py` caches to keep a capture deterministic. They are
# other people's pictures and belong on their own servers, not in here.
test/fixtures/.avatars/

# Editor and OS.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak

# Packaged candidates and Python bytecode.
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local servers and scratch files.
.port
*.local.json
